# Lines NoWayOS's tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial
# lines: the showcase as showcase.qmp types it into QEMU's serial
# port, or through the Pi 5's Debug Probe - the launcher, the visitor
# sign-in opened from it twice, signed in with a pass and sent to reception
# with the service down, the Service desk four times, closed with
# Home, with Cancel, after sending and by the privacy reset, then the pay at
# the pump twice, followed to all done and declined, "Why is this
# secure?", the Screen Compiler gallery round all its screens, and the attract loop, woken by a key, the
# launcher showing again each time;
# each screen as the UI shows it and the theme it draws in, each
# button pressed, what the service stand-in does, and how each session
# ended. Never what was typed.
# Each countdown tick draws its digits' slot alone: the confirmation's
# first is checked here, and any tick drawing more fails the run.
SHOWCASE: app: starting
SHOWCASE: app: ready: a form of 4 steps and 6 fields; the idle warning after 5 s, the reset after 8 s
# The application checks in first, before the UI starts: its
# backend's stand-in answers not approved, then approves it with epoch 2,
# which every attempt's ticket carries.
SHOWCASE: app: checking in: 1
SHOWCASE: app: check-in 1: not approved; awaiting approval, code 3FA1 075C E219 8840
SHOWCASE: app: checking in: 2
SHOWCASE: app: check-in 2: approved, epoch 2; in service
SHOWCASE: ui: starting
SHOWCASE: ui: the display is 1920x1080 Xrgb8888 at scale 2
SHOWCASE: ui: showing launcher
SHOWCASE: ui: theme launcher
